## Build numbers this phase (all from /usr/bin/time -v on the Legion, real measurements)

| Build | Change | Wall time | Peak RSS | Outcome |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| build-postjs-1.log | bake --post-js uno_scripts fix (link-only, no C++ changed) | 4:34.84 | 7.87 GB | SUCCESS |
| build-frameless-1.log | + Qt::FramelessWindowHint (vcl/qt5/QtFrame.cxx) | ~5 min (not centrally timed, same recipe) | — | SUCCESS to build, but broke document-switching (see 0005-REVERTED) |
| build-revert-frameless-1.log | revert QtFrame.cxx | 4:35.60 | 7.35 GB | SUCCESS |

Each of the three builds above is a targeted recompile+relink (not a from-scratch
`make`), consistent with only one .mk/.cxx file changing per step — nowhere near
phase 2's ~40-minute full build.

## 2026-09-27 — Fix pass update: bbSetWorkspaceColor() + 6-file font bundle

Same pinned LibreOffice/core commit (f8941520...). Two new patches applied on top
of 0001-0004 (0005 stays reverted, not applied): patches/0006-workspace-color-live-theming.patch
(desktop/source/app/initjsunoscripting.cxx — new bbSetWorkspaceColor() native hook)
and patches/0007-beebeeb-font-bundle.patch (download.lst, external/more_fonts/
{Module_more_fonts,UnpackedTarball_beebeeb,ExternalPackage_beebeeb,README-beebeeb}.mk/.md,
static/CustomTarget_emscripten_fs_image.mk).

Two builds this pass, both real `make -j12` full builds on the Legion (the
download.lst change forced a `configure` reconfigure both times, so neither was a
pure relink like phase 4's targeted changes above):

| Build | Change | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| build3 (2 attempts) | 0006 (workspace color) only | 1st attempt failed: `make` invoked `autogen.sh`/`emconfigure` without the emsdk env sourced in that shell (a real environment-setup bug in how this session invoked `make`, not a LibreOffice issue) — fixed by sourcing emsdk_env.sh in the same shell before `make` |
| build4 (3 attempts) | + 0007 (font bundle) | 1st attempt: `ExternalPackage_beebeeb.mk` failed — `strip-components` defaults to 1 in `gb_UnpackedTarget_UnpackedTarget`, silently discarding every file from this fork's OWN flat (no wrapping directory) tarball; fixed by passing `0` explicitly. 2nd attempt: `ExternalPackage` step succeeded but `soffice.data`'s byte size didn't change at all — the `ooo_fonts` auto-install aggregation the other fonts rely on isn't wired for this WASM distro; fixed by listing the 6 files explicitly in `static/CustomTarget_emscripten_fs_image.mk`. 3rd attempt: SUCCESS — `soffice.data` grew by exactly 7,524,020 bytes, byte-for-byte matching the 6 new files' combined raw size |

New sha256 (all 8 files re-hashed; only wasm/data/js/metadata actually changed):

```
a2e8b99a71f5759ba32a7455e501a1fcc3612b107a5d3a16f4ff43dfa7cfcc60  soffice.wasm             171,729,584 bytes  (+213 vs phase 4 — new bbSetWorkspaceColor function)
259b3b1807472de24b90a0bfbb1c4bccadbe2dc84741e5d1ae229dac1952c39c  soffice.data             103,840,963 bytes  (+7,524,020 — the 6 new font files)
356c02321c01daf51da73eac58291f2b93237ac79d15a576f73be42b224c0651  soffice.js                   840,558 bytes  (+270 — baked-in preRun/glue for the new export)
884a0f1a2c7d77233a58b91394f1a609ac74da9384a17145348a47e02dad9f7f  soffice.data.js.metadata     214,090 bytes  (file-offset table grew for the 6 new entries)
