Total bundle: 276,658,999 bytes (263.8 MB), up from 269,134,121 (delta = 7,524,878
bytes, matching the font/patch deltas above summed).

Brotli `-q11` (real, this Mac, `.br` siblings gitignored as always):

| file | before this pass | after | delta |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| soffice.wasm | 38,602,455 | 38,516,221 | -86,234 (compression variance, not a regression — content is 213 bytes larger raw) |
| soffice.data | 15,757,226 | 20,316,026 | **+4,558,800** |
| soffice.js | 127,453 | 127,509 | +56 |
| soffice.data.js.metadata | 19,813 | 19,874 | +61 |
| qtloader.js/qtlogo.svg/favicon.ico/qt_soffice.html | 6,930 (unchanged, unchanged, unchanged, unchanged) | 6,930 | 0 |
| **Total** | **54,514,723 (52.0 MB)** | **58,986,184 (56.3 MB)** | **+4,471,461 (4.27 MiB)** |

**The font bundle's real, measured brotli cost inside the actual packaged
soffice.data is 4,558,800 bytes (4.35 MiB)** — close to (and consistent with) the
4,650,417-byte (4.43 MiB) sum of compressing the 6 font files standalone
(external/more_fonts/README-beebeeb.md's own table); the small difference is
normal brotli dictionary-sharing variance between "compressed alone" and
"compressed as part of a larger blob." Both numbers are well under this task's
15 MB ceiling, with ~10.4-10.6 MB of margin — see README-beebeeb.md for why JP-only
(not the full CJK/SC/KR set) was the deliberate choice given that margin.

## 2026-09-27 — Licensing pass (no engine rebuild)

No engine file changed: the eight sha256 lines above (fix-pass section) are still the
current engine. Two notes for whoever rebuilds next:

- patches/0008 now adds an MPL-2.0 header comment to static/emscripten/
  bb-uno-scripts-default.js, and patches/0007 adds one to README-beebeeb.md. The next
  build's soffice.js may therefore differ from the hash recorded above; record the new
  hashes in a new dated section, as usual.
- The bundle's third-party notices file is NOT an engine artifact and is deliberately
  not listed here: web's office-bundle-stage.sh requires every file named in this
  record to exist in the engine directory. It ships from this repo's git-tracked
  bridge/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt (generated by build/make-third-party-notices.sh),
  so git is its integrity guarantee, like bb-office-api.js.
